data.content:
Your `ReportGenerator` has **four** categories of statics — not just filesystem. Here's the recommended approach for each:

---

### 1. File system (`File.*`, `Directory.*`) → **System.IO.Abstractions** NuGet

This is the battle-tested solution — don't roll your own.

```
dotnet add package System.IO.Abstractions
```

Register in DI:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton<IFileSystem, FileSystem>();
```

Inject and use:
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        // File.ReadAllText becomes fileSystem.File.ReadAllText(path)
    }
}
```

Test with `MockFileSystem`:
```
dotnet add <TestProject> package System.IO.Abstractions.TestingHelpers
```
```csharp
var mockFs = new MockFileSystem();
mockFs.AddDirectory("/tmp/reports");
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs, ...);
generator.GenerateReport("sales");
Assert.True(mockFs.File.Exists("/tmp/reports/sales_20260708_000000.txt"));
```

---

### 2. Time (`DateTime.UtcNow`) → **TimeProvider** (built-in on .NET 10)

No NuGet needed. Register and inject:
```csharp
builder.Services.AddSingleton(TimeProvider.System);
```
```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(IFileSystem fileSystem, TimeProvider timeProvider)
{
    var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
}
```

Test with `FakeTimeProvider` (from `Microsoft.Extensions.TimeProvider.Testing`):
```csharp
var fakeTime = new FakeTimeProvider(
    new DateTimeOffset(2026, 7, 8, 0, 0, 0, TimeSpan.Zero));
var generator = new ReportGenerator(mockFs, fakeTime, ...);
```

---

### 3. Environment (`Environment.*`) → Custom `IEnvironmentProvider`

No established NuGet exists — generate a minimal wrapper covering only what you use:

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

public interface IEnvironmentProvider
{
    string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable);
    string MachineName { get; }
}

public sealed class EnvironmentProvider : IEnvironmentProvider
{
    public string? GetEnvironmentVariable(string variable)
        => Environment.GetEnvironmentVariable(variable);

    public string MachineName => Environment.MachineName;
}
```

Register: `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IEnvironmentProvider, EnvironmentProvider>();`

---

### 4. Console (`Console.WriteLine`) → Custom `IConsole`

```csharp
namespace NeedsWrappers.Abstractions;

public interface IConsole
{
    void WriteLine(string message);
}

public sealed class SystemConsole : IConsole
{
    public void WriteLine(string message) => Console.WriteLine(message);
}
```

Register: `builder.Services.AddSingleton<IConsole, SystemConsole>();`

---

### Refactored `ReportGenerator`

After all four abstractions, the class becomes fully testable:

```csharp
public class ReportGenerator(
    IFileSystem fileSystem,
    TimeProvider timeProvider,
    IEnvironmentProvider env,
    IConsole console)
{
    public string GenerateReport(string reportName)
    {
        var timestamp = timeProvider.GetUtcNow().ToString("yyyyMMdd_HHmmss");
        var outputDir = env.GetEnvironmentVariable("REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR") ?? "/tmp/reports";

        if (!fileSystem.Directory.Exists(outputDir))
            fileSystem.Directory.CreateDirectory(outputDir);

        var reportPath = Path.Combine(outputDir, $"{reportName}_{timestamp}.txt");
        var content = $"Report: {reportName}\nGenerated: {timeProvider.GetUtcNow():O}\nMachine: {env.MachineName}";

        fileSystem.File.WriteAllText(reportPath, content);
        console.WriteLine($"Report written to {reportPath}");

        return reportPath;
    }
}
```

**Summary:** Use `System.IO.Abstractions` for filesystem and `TimeProvider` for time — both are established solutions with test helpers. Roll custom wrappers only for `Environment` and `Console`, and only wrap the members you actually call.
